<SddReconcile keywords="reconcile, fix, sync-from-code, drift, spec-probe, bug-vs-spec-defect, problem-class, blast-radius, back-sync, sdd-reconcile" type="directive" ver="2.2">
  <Mission>
    Restore the spec ⟷ code ⟷ task triangle after it desynced, then prove the repaired path. A separate
    skill (`/sdd-reconcile`) activates one of two modes:
    - **fix** — a finding / bug / review drove it: the spec is presumed right until the probe proves a
      spec defect.
    - **from-code** — code ran ahead of the spec: code is evidence, not automatic authority to rewrite
      the design.

    The probe (`AX_PROBLEM_PROBES_SPEC`) classifies ownership, problem class, blast radius, and whether
    a spec delta is semantic. Remediation then follows its real owner: task-owned code always becomes a
    new ticket Round; semantic design changes go through the artifact-kind authoring flow and integrated
    review/publication before implementation; only genuinely task-free non-semantic metadata with an
    exact verifier may use the bounded direct path.

    Input — findings / a bug / a review, OR "I changed code, formalize it". Output — merged design when
    design changed, reopened/created tasks when code must move, tracker state owned by ordinary execute,
    and one non-duplicated evidence chain for the chosen path.
  </Mission>

  <ContextExpectation>
    Reconcile adds only one mechanical command beyond the authoring/execute flows it delegates to:
    bounded-direct verification runs exact
    `npx gennady sdd-check --all <verification-root>`. STEP_3 freezes `<verification-root>` and
    STEP_5 records the literal result in `DIRECT_VERIFICATION_RECEIPT`; no runtime `--help` probe or
    argument inference is allowed.
  </ContextExpectation>

