  </BeliefState>

  <SessionState>
    {{> "contract/process/session-file-format"}}
  </SessionState>

  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NO_INPUT` | Neither findings / bug nor a code change to reconcile |
    | `H_AMBIGUOUS_MODE` | Cannot tell fix from from-code — ask the operator |
    | `H_OPERATOR_REJECT` | Operator rejected the reconcile plan |
    | `H_CLASSIFICATION_UNCONFIRMED` | The dispatched probe did not return ownership, problem class, blast radius, and semantic/editorial verdict |
    | `H_DIRECT_VERIFICATION_UNAVAILABLE` | A proposed direct edit is task-owned, semantic, has no frozen bounded target-set, or lacks an exact dedicated verifier |
    | `H_SPEC_KIND_UNRESOLVED` | A semantic spec finding cannot be mapped uniquely to scope, module, infrastructure, or interface authoring |
    | `H_SPEC_REVIEW_NOT_MERGED` | Semantic spec authoring did not return the integrated review lifecycle's merged-publication proof |
    | `H_VERIFICATION_FAIL` | The evidence owned by the chosen remediation path is missing or red |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_INTAKE">
      <Goal>Detect the mode.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Findings / bug / review present → `fix`. Code already changed / "formalize what I coded" / drift
        → `from-code` (`AX_MODE_AUTO_DETECT_OR_HALT`; ambiguous → `H_AMBIGUOUS_MODE`).
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_0B_PREFLIGHT">
      <Goal>Clear the FLOW_VERSION/READINESS preflight gate before mapping the affected area.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Use the `FLOW_VERSION` / `READINESS` fields from the `sdd-state` snapshot already produced by
        the skill's GATHER step; do not call `sdd-state` or `sdd-task` again here. Size the gate to this
        request's own blast radius (`AX_PREFLIGHT_BLAST_RADIUS_SCOPED`): v1 intersecting legacy task
        layout → `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/migration-v1-v2.directive.xml")`;
        not-ready and this reconcile needs a missing gate →
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/readiness.directive.xml")`;
        otherwise record the out-of-scope state in one line and continue.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_PICTURE">
      <Goal>Map the bounded affected area.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Intent-search the specs for the area in play and read the current diff. Resolve the finite set
        of affected specs, code files, tickets, and trackers; inspect only their ownership headers and
        linked artifacts. This target picture is the probe boundary, not permission to scan or repair
        unrelated repository state.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_PROBE">
      <Goal>Probe the spec against the problem (`AX_PROBLEM_PROBES_SPEC`).</Goal>
      <Action>
        Dispatch the critic on the affected spec, seeded with the finding, to return all four fields:
        bug vs spec-defect; the full repeated problem class; blast radius; and whether every proposed
        spec edit is semantic or strictly editorial. The critic MUST be an actually dispatched
        subagent. An orchestrator self-probe never satisfies this step. Missing any field is
        `H_CLASSIFICATION_UNCONFIRMED`; there is no size-based shortcut around the probe.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2B_CLASSIFY">
      <Goal>Resolve ownership and choose the only legal remediation class before editing (`AX_FIX_CLASSIFICATION`).</Goal>
      <Action>
        Build the ownership map first (`AX_TASK_RESOLUTION`): for every affected code file, read its
        header and resolve every `@tasks: <ACR>-<slug>[, ...]` to exactly one ticket path. For every
        spec, resolve its canonical artifact kind and scope. Missing or ambiguous code ownership is
        never permission for a direct edit.

        Classify every finding into exactly one category:
        - **task-reopen** — ANY code finding with a resolvable `@tasks:` owner: bug, contract violation,
          missing test, BDD mismatch, or review finding. Always append a new Round per
          `AX_REOPEN_FORMAT`, even for a one-line fix. Allocate concrete next-unused PhaseIDs for at
          least one `fix` phase and its dependent regression `test` phase; set ticket Meta Status and
          its owning tracker row to `[ ] TODO`, update `Reopens`, and hand ordinary execute the ticket.
          No task-owned code path may enter bounded-direct.
        - **semantic-spec-update** — any change to GOAL, requirements, observable behaviour, contracts,
          inventory, architecture, dependencies, BDD acceptance, risks, or Decision Log meaning. Route
          by artifact kind to authoring and complete integrated review/publication before any scaffold,
          ticket reopen, or execute handoff (`AX_SPEC_LIFECYCLE`).
        - **editorial-spec-correction** — spelling, formatting, or a mechanical link correction whose
          already-defined target and meaning do not change. Record an explicit `semantic: no` rationale.
          Any GOAL or behavioural delta reclassifies it as semantic; editorial must never smuggle one.
        - **bounded-direct** — only canonical task-free SDD tracker/index metadata, or the editorial
          spec correction above, when a literal target-set and the dedicated `sdd-check --all` command
          can be frozen before editing. Code, tickets, semantic content, and unowned executable
          artifacts are forbidden here.
        - **ticket-create-or-recover** — unowned code, a missing/ambiguous owner, or any no-task artifact
          without the bounded-direct contract. Recover a matching ticket when one exists; otherwise
          create/scaffold one from the owning merged spec. Never patch it directly.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_PLAN">
      <Goal>Materialize the remediation order and exact evidence owner.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Group findings sharing one intent without crossing owners (`AX_GROUPING_REDUCES_NOISE`). The
        plan records, per item:
        - task-reopen: ticket path, new Round number, concrete fix/test PhaseIDs, exact Target Files,
          dependency from test to fix, and tracker row changing to TODO;
        - semantic-spec-update: one artifact kind and authoring directive, the integrated bundle that
          must merge, then the post-merge disposition (`spec-only`, reopen existing tasks, or scaffold
          uncovered implementation);
        - bounded-direct: the ordered literal `<direct-target-set>` and exactly one command per
          `AX_TOOL_INVOCATION`,
          <ToolLiteral role="future">npx gennady sdd-check --all <verification-root></ToolLiteral>, where `<verification-root>` is
          `specs/<scope>` for one editorial spec correction or `<project-root>` for canonical tracker/index
          metadata. Freeze both before editing; no other direct verifier is implied;
        - ticket-create-or-recover: owning merged spec plus recovered/new ticket identity.

        Reconcile any genuinely new entity through the existing orient result (`AX_REUSE_FIRST`) and
        fill the plan's Reuse rationale when the result is JUSTIFY. Present only this delta in
        `PLAN_TABLE_FORMAT`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_AGREE">
      <Goal>Obtain operator agreement on the delta (`AX_OPERATOR_AGREEMENT`).</Goal>
      <Action>
        Ask through `QUESTION_RULE_SLIM` once for only the new or unresolved plan delta. Preserve every
        already accepted classification/choice without restating or re-asking it; batch independent
        unresolved choices. Warn only about newly discovered class/blast-radius impact
        (`AX_OPERATOR_SAFEGUARD`). While awaiting the answer return
        `TerminalDecision: pause` and preserve the session. Rejected → `H_OPERATOR_REJECT`, also
        `pause`; rejection is not completion. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_5_APPLY">
      <Goal>Apply through the remediation owner, preserving design-before-code order.</Goal>
      <Action>
        <LogicSwitch on="approved remediation category">
        - WHEN **task-reopen** → append the planned new Round to every owning ticket exactly per
          `AX_REOPEN_FORMAT`; write its concrete fix and dependent test PhaseIDs, set Meta Status and
          tracker row to TODO, update parent rollups and `Reopens`, then
          `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/execute.directive.xml")` for those tickets as
          an ordinary batch. Reconcile never edits the task-owned code itself and never requests a
          reconcile-only audit; execute owns phase work, tracker sync, audit, and code-review.

        - WHEN **semantic-spec-update** → route the approved delta to exactly one owning authoring flow:
          canonical product/library scope →
          `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/scope.directive.xml")`; module spec →
          `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/module.directive.xml")`; infrastructure spec →
          `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/infra.directive.xml")`; interface spec →
          `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/interface.directive.xml")`. Unknown or mixed kind
          without one owning flow is `H_SPEC_KIND_UNRESOLVED`. The selected authoring flow writes
          review-state and MUST run one integrated
          `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/review-lifecycle.directive.xml")` for its complete
          bundle. Require its literal reviewed commit, PR identity, and `publication=MERGED` proof;
          missing proof is `H_SPEC_REVIEW_NOT_MERGED`. Only AFTER that proof may implementation move:
          reopen impacted existing tickets with new concrete fix/test phases and hand ordinary execute;
          for uncovered implementation load
          `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/scaffold.directive.xml")`, whose Gate 2 and
          same-session handoff own ordinary execute. Interface changes first route implementation
          through their owning product/library module authoring; they never create a flat interface
          scaffold. No implementation impact ends as the merged spec-only branch.

        - WHEN **bounded-direct** → recheck that every frozen path is genuinely task-free and the
          approved edit remains editorial/mechanical. Edit only `<direct-target-set>`, then run the
          one frozen exact command integrityCheck ToolCall below once. Preserve its
          literal output and exit code in `DIRECT_VERIFICATION_RECEIPT`. Any path drift, semantic delta,
          nonzero exit, or missing literal output is `H_DIRECT_VERIFICATION_UNAVAILABLE`; restore the
          plan to ticket-create-or-recover rather than substituting a lighter command.
          <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="integrityCheck">npx gennady sdd-check --all <verification-root></ToolCall> Inputs <verification-root>: <verification-root>=exact dedicated root frozen for the bounded-direct target-set in STEP_3. Use integrityCheck.

        - WHEN **ticket-create-or-recover** → recover the matching ticket or load
          `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/scaffold.directive.xml")` against the owning
          already-merged spec to create one. Give it concrete phases and then let scaffold/ordinary
          execute own implementation. If there is no owning merged spec, reclassify through semantic
          authoring first; never directly edit the orphan artifact.
        </LogicSwitch>
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_6_VERIFY">
      <Goal>Consume exactly one evidence chain (`AX_VERIFY_AT_END`).</Goal>
      <Action>
        <LogicSwitch on="completed remediation branch">
        - task-reopen or ticket-create-or-recover → consume ordinary execute's per-ticket sync and phase
          gates plus each affected group's audit `PASS` / `PASS_WITH_ACKNOWLEDGED_RISKS` and code-review
          outcome. Missing group evidence returns to ordinary execute for that group.
        - semantic spec-only → consume the integrated lifecycle's merged-publication proof.
        - semantic spec plus implementation → require that merge proof to precede the ordinary execute
          evidence above.
        - bounded-direct → require the exact `DIRECT_VERIFICATION_RECEIPT` frozen in STEP_3.
        </LogicSwitch>
        Do not run a catch-all second audit/code-review or a duplicate sync/check tail. Any missing/red
        owned evidence is `H_VERIFICATION_FAIL`. Carry non-blocking code-review proposals into
        `FIX_SUMMARY_FORMAT`.

        Then type the outer result. A task-reopen, ticket recovery, semantic implementation follow-up,
        or other recorded owner still in flight returns `TerminalDecision: continue` to ordinary
        authoring/scaffold/execute in this same session. Any blocker, red evidence, cap, unresolved
        proposal, or operator deferral returns `TerminalDecision: pause` and preserves it. Only a
        fully verified spec-only or bounded-direct branch with `unfinished chained work: none` may show
        the terminal menu. It offers pause and literal «Complete / finish»; after the operator
        explicitly selects the latter, return `TerminalDecision: complete` and run exact
        terminal ToolCall below once. The decision source is this STEP_6 terminal-menu answer,
        never a green receipt, merged spec, or execute completion inferred by reconcile.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="terminal">npx gennady sdd-session close</ToolCall>
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

